 Business Proposal & Technical Overview

 Project Name: EzYir Soya Web Store & Delivery Platform
 Location: Asante Akyem South, Ghana

 Prepared For: EzYir Soya Store Management

 Date: September 2026



 Summary

 The EzYir Soya Web Store is a lightweight, responsive digital e-commerce platform designed to bring premium organic soya products
  directly to retail and wholesale customers across Asante Akyem South and surrounding areas. By combining an online store layout,
   flexible scheduling options, and payment gateway integration, the platform expands market reach for individual orders, bulk supply, 
   and event catering.   

Bussiness Objectives
Digital Storefront: Showcase EzYir’s natural soya beverage and plant-based protein catalog online. 
Order & Event Scheduling: Enable customers to schedule deliveries or pickups up to 3 weeks (21 days) in advance for personal use,
 commercial supply, or events (weddings, parties, funerals).  
Payment Processing: Integrate Paystack Inline JS to support payments via Mobile Money (MoMo) and bank cards.   

Operational Efficiency: Streamline logistics through structured checkout forms capturing contact information, 
fulfillment options, and delivery schedules.   

 

 Technical & Functional 
 Features1.
  Frontend ArchitectureHTML5 & CSS3: Structured layout featuring navigation, hero section, grid system for products,
 and side-panel shopping cart.  

  Responsive Navigation: Mobile hamburger menu toggle for smartphones and tablets.  


  2. Shopping Cart & Dynamic Scheduling (JavaScript)Interactive Cart Engine:
   Functions to add, increment, decrement, or remove items with automatic total updates.  
   
    Automated Date Selector: Restricts booking options from tomorrow up to a 21-day window to maintain order fulfillment timelines.
Cutoff Time Monitoring: Banner notification alerts customers when orders are placed during evening hours (4:40 PM – 12:30 AM),
 ensuring clear delivery expectations. 



 3. Payment Gateway IntegrationUses Paystack's Inline JavaScript SDK to trigger a payment popup directly on checkout. 
Attaches metadata (customer phone number, fulfillment type, and scheduled delivery date) to each transaction reference for fulfillment
 processing. 


 Operating Policies & TermsDelivery Fee: Variable by destination, confirmed via direct phone call prior to dispatch. 
Fulfillment Modes: Choice of Home/Site Delivery or Self Pickup. 

  Refund Policy: Strict no-refund policy once an order has been placed and payment is processed



  Recommended Next Steps for Implementation
Backend Integration & Webhooks: Connect Paystack webhooks to a Node.js backend server to record transaction records in a database.

Automated SMS Notifications: Connect an SMS API (such as Hubtel, Termii, or Twilio) to dispatch automated order confirmations
 to both customer and store managers upon payment success.

Paystack Production Activation: Switch from Paystack test key (pk_test_...) to live merchant credentials (pk_live_...) upon business 
verification.   













